WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.050
[NARRATOR]
There once was
a man named Mont Blanc Noland.

3
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:56.010
<b>North Blue The Kingdom of Lvneel</b>

4
00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.550
He was from a kingdom
in the Northern seas.

5
00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:04.270
<b>Raigo</b>

6
00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.840
Noland, or "Noland the Explorer,"

7
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.180
always told stories about
his incredible adventures.

8
00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.410
They were so incredible
that the villagers

9
00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.620
could never tell if
they were true or not.

10
00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:15.870
One day, Noland returned from a long
journey to report to the king.

11
00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:19.340
[NOLAND]
It stands proud and beautiful in ruin!

12
00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.020
The city is named Shandora!

13
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.190
But they call it "The City of Gold,"

14
00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.150
which describes it perfectly.

15
00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:27.820
[KING, COUNSELOR laugh]

16
00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.460
<b>Five Years Later</b>

17
00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.470
[KING]
Marie Jois has finally granted us
permission to enter the Grand Line.

18
00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.100
So I would like to send
you on another mission.

19
00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.810
It would be my pleasure.

20
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.290
[KING]
There will be a slight change, however.

21
00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:43.920
This time, my soldiers
and I will accompany you.

22
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:46.900
Is that understood?

23
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.900
Yes.

24
00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.940
<b>One Year Before Noland's Arrival</b>

25
00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.400
[SETO]
Kalgara!

26
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.400
[KALGARA]
Seto.

27
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.280
[SETO]
You're off to ring the bell, right?

28
00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.820
I'll help you.

29
00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.220
[NOLA hisses]

30
00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.570
[SETO chuckles]
It's good to see you too, Nola!

31
00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:04.450
You sure have made yourself at
home in these ruins, haven't you?

32
00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.330
Hey, when do you think Noland and
the rest of his crew are coming back?

33
00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.800
[KALGARA chuckles]

34
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.290
That's all you ever ask
about when we come here.

35
00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.090
It's not exactly easy
for him to return.

36
00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.300
He was born all the way
in the far northern seas.

37
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.310
He also has a family back home.

38
00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.180
But... he promised.

39
00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.650
As long as we keep ringing
this bell the way we have been,

40
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.070
he'll show up again someday.

41
00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.490
[SOUTHBIRD calls]

42
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.020
[KALGARA]
What's happened to the sky?

43
00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.280
Come on, Seto!

44
00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.990
We have to protect the village!

45
00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:02.430
<b>November 16, 1127
The Pelagic Calendar</b>

46
00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.640
[NOLAND]
Why?

47
00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:07.810
Why does the island suddenly end here?

48
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.100
[NOLAND grunts]

49
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.400
Damn you, Noland!

50
00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.860
I cannot believe I ever
trusted you. You liar!

51
00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.430
Where is the city of gold you
promised I would find here?

52
00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.530
[NOLAND]
Where did the village go?

53
00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.850
What happened to the island?

54
00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:28.880
Kalgara, if you're alive,
please ring the golden bell!

55
00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.630
Answer me, fire of Shandora!

56
00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:39.010
<b>The Kingdom of Lvneel</b>

57
00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.010
[CITIZEN A]
Noland's public
execution is about to start!

58
00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.220
Hey! It's this way, guys!

59
00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:43.890
[NOLAND]
It's true.

60
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:48.480
I saw a giant city of gold on
the Grand Line island of Jaya.

61
00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:52.220
The City of Gold
does exist, I assure you.

62
00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.510
[JUDGE]
Let us hear from one of your crew.

63
00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:57.040
Is this man telling the truth?

64
00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.530
He's not. It's an absolute lie.

65
00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.070
No! Please.

66
00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.990
You can't trust anything that man says!

67
00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.330
He's a liar!

68
00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.000
[GIRL CITIZEN A]
Were all his stories fake?

69
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.340
Hey, that's not fair!

70
00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.040
He's been lying to the whole
kingdom and acting like a hero!

71
00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.090
Wait, hold on!
Where'd you get that witness?

72
00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.800
He's not even part of our crew!

73
00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.210
Did you happen to see
Kalgara and the others?

74
00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:21.050
[SAILOR EE]
Commodore! What happened?

75
00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.720
Seize all of them!

76
00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.560
[SAILORS gasp]

77
00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.760
[SAILOR EE]
Damn it!

78
00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.810
Leave my men alone.

79
00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.380
[JUDGE clears throat]

80
00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:36.470
For his heinous lies, Mont Blanc Noland is
hereby sentenced to death by beheading!

81
00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.030
Liar!

82
00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:46.810
[CITIZENS yelling]

83
00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:47.940
[SAILOR XX]
Noland!

84
00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.110
[CITIZENS yelling]

85
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.260
[CITIZENS]
– Liar! Liar!
– Liar! Liar!

86
00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:58.680
Liar! Liar!

87
00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.060
[chanting continues]

88
00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:46.260
Look at that! A giant island of Vearth!

89
00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.210
[GOD]
Can you hear that?

90
00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.470
The singing voice of
this beautiful Vearth.

91
00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:54.940
It is truly the birth of holy land.

92
00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.020
This is definitely where I must live.

93
00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.480
[KALGARA]
What's going on here?

94
00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.050
What happened?

95
00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.510
Why can't I breathe?

96
00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.660
[WARRIOR B]
Is everybody all right?

97
00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:09.780
[WARRIOR F]
Pull yourselves together!

98
00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.080
[WARRIOR G]
Come on, everyone! Get up!

99
00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.750
[WARRIOR E]
Tend to the wounded! Hurry!

100
00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.100
[WARRIOR H]
Kalgara!

101
00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.400
I hereby claim this Vearth as mine!

102
00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.110
You will call me God!

103
00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.830
[KALGARA]
You are not God!

104
00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.750
Shandorians, we fight!

105
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.000
[WARRIORS yell]

106
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.010
We cannot let them take our land!

107
00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.380
[WARRIORS yelling]

108
00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.760
[KALGARA]
We made a promise, Noland.

109
00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.390
We promised we would
meet again someday.

110
00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:42.260
[NOLAND]
Kalgara... where are you?

111
00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:47.640
[KALGARA]
When you finally return, what will
you think when you see we're gone?

112
00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.620
Hold on a little longer!

113
00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.690
I'll let you know
that we're still here!

114
00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.450
[NOLAND]
Are you alive?

115
00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:01.540
[KALGARA]
I have so much to tell you!

116
00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:03.730
[NOLAND]
Kalgara!

117
00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.820
I have to know if you're all right!

118
00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:11.910
[KALGARA]
Let's meet again
on the same land one day!

119
00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.100
Noland!

120
00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.130
Light the fire of Shandora!

121
00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.720
[CHIEFTAIN]
And the great Warrior
Kalgara continued to shout.

122
00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.300
Just once would've been enough.

123
00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.350
But he believed that
the Fire of Shandora

124
00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:32.140
would echo and tell
the world that we are here.

125
00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.650
But the bell never rang once.

126
00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:38.020
And then, everything was
explained to our villagers.

127
00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:44.800
Sailors from the Blue Sea told us
that Noland, to whom we owe so much,

128
00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:49.100
had such pride for our city
that he refused to deny

129
00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:53.980
Shandora's existence
and died known as a liar.

130
00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.480
But it was too late.

131
00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:04.070
The great warrior Kalgara had died
honorably in battle here in the sky.

132
00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.150
He was never able
to convey his message.

133
00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:11.560
And that was the Great
Warrior's biggest regret.

134
00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.660
[WYPER]
Do you think we'd
still be able to reach him?

135
00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:17.860
If we rang the bell now, do you think
we'd be able to still reach Noland?

136
00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:19.070
Tell me the truth!

137
00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.460
That's a good question.

138
00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.500
Well, we are close to Heaven.

139
00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.670
[AISA]
Wyper! Come on!

140
00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.460
We'll die if we don't leave now!

141
00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.280
Please, Wyper!

142
00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:37.820
[WYPER]
Eneru!

143
00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.770
What gives you the right to
take away everything we know?

144
00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:45.610
[ENERU laughing]

145
00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:48.690
This is the sky! It is God's domain!

146
00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.360
Everything is an eyesore!

147
00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:55.660
The people, the trees, the land!
Return to where you belong!

148
00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.990
Let everything rain into the Blue Sea!

149
00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:03.820
Get to the boats!

150
00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.130
Angel Island won't last much longer!

151
00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.510
Sir, what do we do with the
people who've been injured?

152
00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:11.760
Hurry! We'll treat them
once they're in the boats.

153
00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:18.430
[CROWD yelling]

154
00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:22.020
[MCKINLEY]
What would've happened if that
girl had approached me any later?

155
00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:24.440
I hope she's all right.

156
00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:40.590
The little angels will
scurry like the ants they are!

157
00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:46.930
Return to where you belong, Skypiea!

158
00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.400
[CROWD screaming]

159
00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.050
[SKY PERSON A]
What is that?

160
00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:53.900
[SKY PERSON B]
A hole in the White White Sea?

161
00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:58.150
[ENERU]
I have no need for
God's Shrine anymore, either!

162
00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.320
[laughing]

163
00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:05.740
The city of Shandora
is useless to me as well!

164
00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:19.820
There is only one thing
in this land that I want.

165
00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:23.910
The gold belfry!

166
00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.080
Suddenly I hear two voices.

167
00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.960
[NAMI]
How can he run so fast?

168
00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.620
[LUFFY]
Hang in there, Nami.

169
00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.620
I'll take care of this I promise!

170
00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.960
Eneru! I'll never let you
have the golden bell!

171
00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.390
I don't get it.

172
00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.560
What is it that Eneru wants there?

173
00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.110
I believe he's trying
to get to the golden bell.

174
00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.390
A bell?

175
00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.270
[WYPER]
A golden bell.

176
00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:00.650
[USOPP gasps]

177
00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:01.730
[WYPER]
Tell me.

178
00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:03.310
That's what you said, isn't it.

179
00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.440
[AISA]
Wyper!

180
00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.280
[ROBIN]
Yes.

181
00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.730
[USOPP]
Uh... uh...

182
00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.820
Who was talking about a golden bell?

183
00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:11.170
Just before you were
struck by that lightning bolt,

184
00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.810
you were speaking of a golden
bell which Eneru desires.

185
00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:19.650
Now that we know what Eneru's going for,
you have to tell me where it is.

186
00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:23.750
[USOPP]
Mmm... Hold on, could we just think
about this for one second, guys?!

187
00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:25.270
You saw that thunderbolt!

188
00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:28.390
We're as good as dead
if we don't get out of here!

189
00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:32.500
It's up this beanstalk.

190
00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.420
Somewhere close to the top.

191
00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:36.320
You're sure? How do you know this?

192
00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:37.370
[USOPP]
Wait!

193
00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.910
We promised Nami that we'd
wait back on the ship!

194
00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:44.670
She's gonna be back
with Luffy any time now!

195
00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:46.210
I'm sure!

196
00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.160
The coward's right this time!

197
00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:51.920
The ruins of Shandora are in
the layer directly beneath us.

198
00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:55.960
The giant beanstalk pierces
the very center of the city.

199
00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.710
[USOPP]
Oh, man!

200
00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.540
These ruins or whatever
they are got blasted to dust!

201
00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.880
And if we don't get outta here
right now, we're gonna be next!

202
00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.090
[ROBIN]
In the ruins, I
discovered a map that revealed

203
00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:13.260
the location of the grand belfry
that holds the golden bell.

204
00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:16.470
It indicated that it could be found
in the heart of the ancient city.

205
00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:18.770
[ROBIN]
To put it simply,
the force of the impact

206
00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:22.900
with the vine must have sent the bell
hurling skyward to its present location.

207
00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:39.530
[LUFFY]
Hey!

208
00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:47.410
The City of Gold's got
a really big bell in it, right?

209
00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:48.620
[chuckles]

210
00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:58.090
Finally. I'm above Giant Jack.

211
00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.340
Virgin sky.

212
00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:01.430
I certainly never had
reason to come up here

213
00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:04.510
and I doubt anyone else
has either... now where is it?

214
00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.990
After 400 years...

215
00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:10.600
...it will be found.

216
00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.830
The golden bell.

217
00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:35.810
[ENERU]
Him.

218
00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:40.150
It would appear that I
underestimated the little rat.

219
00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.020
Ha! Gotcha!

220
00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.490
Stay right there!

221
00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:49.360
Eneru!

222
00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.120
Absurd.

223
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.540
[LUFFY grunts, yells]

224
00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:07.340
[yelling]

225
00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.970
[ENERU laughs]

226
00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.640
[LUFFY yelling]

227
00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:17.100
Uh, Wyper?

228
00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.690
What're you planning to do?

229
00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.190
Don't tell me you're gonna
climb the beanstalk!

230
00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:28.030
Everyone! Get away from the beanstalk!

231
00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:29.910
Something's falling!

232
00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:32.570
[USOPP yells]

233
00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:35.290
[AISA yells]

234
00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:38.880
The top of the stalk!

235
00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.460
What's happening up there?

236
00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:42.970
Oh, no! Don't tell me
Luffy and Nami fell with it!

237
00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:44.590
I just don't think I could take it!

238
00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:45.800
[AISA]
Wyper!

239
00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.120
[WYPER groans]

240
00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.910
[AISA]
No! You can't go!

241
00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.330
Not in this condition!

242
00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.040
Look at yourself, you're a wreck!

243
00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.420
You'd never make it!

244
00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:57.420
And even if you did, there's no way to reach
Eneru while he's flying on that ship!

245
00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:00.840
The bell. It's directly above us.

246
00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:07.560
Great Warrior Kalgara
longed to hear its sound.

247
00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.320
This little predicament
will make it very difficult

248
00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:21.740
indeed for you to reach me, won't it?

249
00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:22.910
[LUFFY grunts]

250
00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.410
You just wait!

251
00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.410
[grunting]

252
00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.810
Hang around a little bit longer...

253
00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.260
...and I'll show you
something miraculous.

254
00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:36.360
Show you... something...?

255
00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:42.790
What is all that?

256
00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:47.300
Oh, yeah.

257
00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:49.510
I guess I should get out of
this while he's not around.

258
00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.110
[NAMI]
What is he doing?!

259
00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.320
[LUFFY grunting]

260
00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:31.910
Wow. My plan totally worked!

261
00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.750
All right, now's my chance
to get on board that ark!

262
00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:35.960
[grunts]

263
00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:39.710
Luffy!

264
00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:42.830
What are you doing here, Nami?
I haven't rescued you yet.

265
00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.710
I came to rescue you, you dolt!

266
00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:49.530
Sanji and Usopp saved me so I was
safe down below this whole time.

267
00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:53.240
Really? You were? That's great.

268
00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:54.530
I was worried.

269
00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.510
More importantly...

270
00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:57.970
Wait.

271
00:17:58.900 --> 00:17:59.900
What's that?

272
00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:01.520
[rumbling continues]

273
00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:05.900
The thunderclouds.

274
00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.450
They're changing shape.

275
00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:15.380
[SKY PERSON A, B]
– The sky! Save us!
– The sky! Save us!

276
00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:17.470
[SKY PERSON C]
Oh, no! Somebody please help us!

277
00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:19.380
[SKY PERSON D]
The sky! It's pitch black!

278
00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:20.680
[WOMAN]
What's happening?

279
00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:21.760
[DAUGHTER]
Mama!

280
00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.050
Move it! Everyone to the sea!

281
00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:26.140
[SKY PEOPLE yelling]

282
00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:28.770
[SKY PERSON E]
There's a giant
ball floating in the sky!

283
00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:31.310
[SKY PEOPLE yelling]

284
00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.730
I have a bad feeling about this.

285
00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:40.220
That ball coming through the clouds
over there is a massive thunderhead.

286
00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:44.440
And it's bursting at the seams with
hurricane winds and deadly lightning bolts.

287
00:18:57.370 --> 00:19:00.410
It's right above... Angel Island!

288
00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.660
A thundercloud shaped like a sphere.

289
00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.550
Unreal...

290
00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:08.840
This has got to be a nightmare.

291
00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:11.760
[GAN FALL]
What is this?

292
00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:14.600
What new horrors could he unleash next?

293
00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:21.420
[SKY PERSON F]
Hurry! Get to the ocean!

294
00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.670
[SKY PERSON G]
Wait for me!

295
00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:32.100
[ENERU laughs]

296
00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.100
Now everyone will know
that the skies are mine!

297
00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:41.980
With the powers of the ark, Maxim,
and myself, I am unstoppable!

298
00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:45.280
I have become truly omnipotent!

299
00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.490
[SKY PERSON H]
Look!

300
00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.860
[SKY PERSON I]
It's falling onto Angel Island!

301
00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.320
[SKY PEOPLE chattering]

302
00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:51.830
[SKY PERSON J]
It's too late!

303
00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.370
[SKY PERSON K]
We're not gonna make it!

304
00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.580
[SKY PERSON L]
Hurry! Everybody run!

305
00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:37.010
I don't believe it. That's impossible!

306
00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:39.050
[SKY PERSON N]
Did the White Berets escape?

307
00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:42.060
[SKY PERSON O]
The White Berets saved us all.

308
00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:45.350
The entire island has been destroyed.

309
00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:47.770
Our precious homeland is gone forever!

310
00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:53.630
[SKY PERSON M]
Even the sea clouds were obliterated.

311
00:20:57.090 --> 00:21:00.800
[ENERU laughing]

312
00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:03.220
What a glorious sight to behold!

313
00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:06.450
Now this is what the
sky should look like.

314
00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.630
[USOPP]
Wh-What kind of explosion was that?

315
00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:19.270
Not to mention, that terrible lightning
is still falling down like rain!

316
00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:22.900
I don't think any of us stand
a chance of getting out of here alive!

317
00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.440
Angel Island's gone.

318
00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.320
How could you?

319
00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:28.480
Eneru...

320
00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.490
What cruelty.

321
00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:34.870
What monstrous cruelty!

322
00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.120
What is that rumbling?

323
00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:44.620
[SUU]
Suu! Suu...

324
00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.450
We'll wait.

325
00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:49.500
We have to take them back
safely to the Blue Sea.

326
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:52.040
[NAMI]
Luffy!

327
00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.210
Get on so we can get back down there!

328
00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:57.380
Everyone else is headed for
the ship and we should be too!

329
00:21:58.720 --> 00:21:59.420
I can't.

330
00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:00.800
Can't? Why not?

331
00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:02.050
What are you saying?

332
00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.510
Yeah, you can.

333
00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:05.970
I don't have to save
you anymore, but...

334
00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:08.720
I still have some unfinished business!

335
00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:11.850
Unfinished business?
What's left to do here?

336
00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:13.900
Are you trying to get back at Eneru?

337
00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:16.980
That golden bell is somewhere
up there in the sky!

338
00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:20.000
You're after the bell? Luffy!

339
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:22.540
Your life is more important than gold.

340
00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:23.920
Look at that!

341
00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:25.910
Even if the lightning doesn't hurt you,

342
00:22:25.910 --> 00:22:30.470
he can still destroy you
a thousand other ways!

343
00:22:30.470 --> 00:22:33.760
If it's gold you want, you have
a load of it on your arm!

344
00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:36.640
So give up the bell, Luffy,
for your own sake!

345
00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:40.090
I won't die.

346
00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:44.830
Will you quit it, already?
You know that he... You saw it, right?

347
00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:46.080
Saw what?

348
00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:52.180
The City of Gold.

349
00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:54.470
You know for a fact it exists, right?

350
00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:01.110
Then it wasn't a lie!

351
00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:04.840
[LUFFY]
Old Timer's ancestor.

352
00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:10.910
[CRICKET]
I don't care if I find the city or not.

353
00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:13.580
I'm not here to prove
Noland right or wrong.

354
00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:16.830
I have no interest
in rewriting history.

355
00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:20.290
All I'm doing is following
what I believe is my destiny.

356
00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:22.510
This is between me and Noland.

357
00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:23.970
[LUFFY]
He wasn't a liar.

358
00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:30.100
I have to let Old Timer and
the others down below know...

359
00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:35.270
...that the City of Gold
is up in the sky!

360
00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:40.900
If I ring the bell...

361
00:23:42.030 --> 00:23:43.780
...then they should be able to hear it.

362
00:23:44.470 --> 00:23:46.560
Otherwise, Old Timer
and his monkey pals

363
00:23:46.560 --> 00:23:49.600
will keep searching the ocean
floor until the day they die!

364
00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:55.460
[NAMI]
Luffy...

365
00:23:56.690 --> 00:23:59.490
Eneru won't take the golden bell.

366
00:23:59.490 --> 00:24:04.210
The sound from a bell that huge will be
heard far and wide by people everywhere.

367
00:24:05.730 --> 00:24:09.940
So I'm not stopping until I hear
the sounds of the golden bell!

368
00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:15.890
[LUFFY]
The City of Gold's got
a really big bell in it, right?

369
00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:21.410
Noland did mention
that in his logbook, yes.

370
00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:24.410
A great bell in the City of Gold.

371
00:24:24.410 --> 00:24:25.790
Why do you ask, Luffy?

372
00:24:25.790 --> 00:24:27.620
Yeah, why do you ask, Luffy?

373
00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:29.380
[LUFFY chuckling]

374
00:24:29.380 --> 00:24:31.090
I got a really good idea.

375
00:24:32.670 --> 00:24:34.930
Well, tell me!

376
00:24:34.930 --> 00:24:37.800
If we give that ginormous
bell a good ringing,

377
00:24:37.800 --> 00:24:42.050
I bet that Old Timer and those monkeys
down below would hear it. Don'tcha think?

378
00:24:42.050 --> 00:24:43.970
[chuckles]

379
00:24:45.470 --> 00:24:47.390
Yeah, I bet they would.

380
00:24:50.390 --> 00:24:53.300
When he says that he's
gonna do something, he does it.

381
00:24:53.370 --> 00:24:55.250
Wait. He's gonna...

382
00:24:56.350 --> 00:24:58.230
Yes, he did say that.

383
00:24:58.230 --> 00:25:00.350
But given the situation...

384
00:25:03.790 --> 00:25:05.590
[WYPER]
Ring?

385
00:25:05.610 --> 00:25:07.780
He's going to ring the bell?

386
00:25:08.210 --> 00:25:09.090
That's right.

387
00:25:09.090 --> 00:25:14.010
No matter how hard Nami tries, Luffy
won't leave until he rings that bell.

388
00:25:14.030 --> 00:25:17.950
You see, Luffy is after
the same thing as Eneru.

389
00:25:27.280 --> 00:25:28.410
Got it!

390
00:25:30.950 --> 00:25:32.280
[ENERU laughs]

391
00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:36.200
As captain of this ship, I do
not give you permission to board.

392
00:25:36.510 --> 00:25:37.600
Eneru!

393
00:25:39.540 --> 00:25:42.920
[LUFFY yelling]

394
00:25:46.370 --> 00:25:47.500
[NAMI]
Luffy!

395
00:25:47.500 --> 00:25:51.020
See, I told you that was a bad idea!

396
00:25:51.020 --> 00:25:52.230
Damn him!

397
00:25:52.230 --> 00:25:53.430
[ENERU laughs]

398
00:25:53.430 --> 00:25:54.890
Wasn't it beautiful?

399
00:25:54.890 --> 00:25:59.290
Did you get to see that pathetic
little island vanish from the sky?

400
00:25:59.290 --> 00:26:01.120
I can only assume
that you are acquainted

401
00:26:01.120 --> 00:26:04.570
with how forgiving I am, especially
to those who would deceive me.

402
00:26:04.570 --> 00:26:07.370
Girl, would you still
like a trip to Endless Vearth?

403
00:26:07.370 --> 00:26:08.660
Not a chance!

404
00:26:08.660 --> 00:26:12.050
Once I have finally found the treasured
relic I've been searching for,

405
00:26:12.050 --> 00:26:14.800
I will use another
devastating Raigo to annihilate

406
00:26:14.800 --> 00:26:17.540
the rest of this abominable
island in the sky!

407
00:26:17.540 --> 00:26:21.630
Then every inhabitant of Skypiea
will suffer my terrible wrath!

408
00:26:25.890 --> 00:26:30.470
[ENERU]
All will perish, including
the voices directly beneath you.

409
00:26:30.470 --> 00:26:32.020
Beneath us?

410
00:26:32.020 --> 00:26:37.300
I will eradicate this unnatural
land in the sky once and for all!

411
00:26:37.300 --> 00:26:41.890
I will change everything back
to the way it was intended!

412
00:26:42.870 --> 00:26:47.000
That... is my sacred
duty as Eneru Almighty!

413
00:26:53.510 --> 00:26:55.720
I'm not gonna let that happen!

414
00:26:55.720 --> 00:26:59.600
You won't get away with this!

415
00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:05.570
[LUFFY yelling]

416
00:27:05.570 --> 00:27:06.900
[ENERU laughs]

417
00:27:06.900 --> 00:27:09.820
Your time ends now, rubber boy!

418
00:27:10.530 --> 00:27:12.490
Die with dignity!

419
00:27:15.950 --> 00:27:16.490
[NAMI]
Luffy!

420
00:27:17.660 --> 00:27:19.120
[LUFFY growls]

421
00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:21.080
[LUFFY yells]

422
00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:24.660
Luffy!

423
00:27:28.630 --> 00:27:30.260
Face it.

424
00:27:30.260 --> 00:27:32.840
It's beyond anyone's
power to stop me now.

425
00:27:35.890 --> 00:27:37.310
[LUFFY growls]

426
00:27:37.310 --> 00:27:40.190
Eneru...!

427
00:27:40.190 --> 00:27:42.730
[CRICKET]
Listen, everything will be all right.

428
00:27:42.730 --> 00:27:45.030
I promise. We will send you to the sky.

429
00:27:51.730 --> 00:27:53.030
Luffy...

430
00:27:55.950 --> 00:27:58.450
[LUFFY]
I'm gonna...

431
00:28:02.190 --> 00:28:05.820
...ring that bell!

432
00:28:13.730 --> 00:28:19.250
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

433
00:28:19.470 --> 00:28:24.670
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

434
00:28:24.670 --> 00:28:27.470
You are so much like the moon

435
00:28:27.470 --> 00:28:32.120
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

436
00:28:35.570 --> 00:28:44.520
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

437
00:28:44.580 --> 00:28:49.750
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

438
00:28:49.750 --> 00:28:58.060
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

439
00:28:58.700 --> 00:29:04.950
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

440
00:29:04.950 --> 00:29:10.570
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

441
00:29:11.810 --> 00:29:16.340
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

442
00:29:16.340 --> 00:29:22.730
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
